    {
      "run": 4,
      "steps": 12,
      "narrative": "I found myself in a small, cramped galley, the air thick with salt. The kettle, my initial objective, lay on the floor, a speck amidst the clutter. I picked it up, its weight comforting in my grasp. I then ventured north, only to return and finish my inspection. The southern hatch piqued my curiosity, and I opened it, finding myself descending into darkness. I descended, exploring the depths, and upon resurfacing, looked around, taking in the familiar galleyscape - the north doorway, the salty floor, the hatch, and the kettle. It was a peculiar expedition, filled with exploration and discovery in this maritime enclave.",
